.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt IMT 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm imt
.Nd I2C Windows Precision Touchpad pointer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "imt* at ihidev?"
.Cd "wsmouse* at imt? mux 0"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver reads Windows Precision Touchpad contact reports through
.Xr ihidev 4 .
It sends relative pointer motion and the physical left button to
.Xr wsmouse 4 .
It can generate a left click from a short single-finger tap.
.Pp
The driver requires complete parallel contact reports.
It rejects frames with an invalid size, excessive contact count,
duplicate contact identifiers, or coordinates outside the descriptor ranges.
.Pp
The driver selects Precision Touchpad input mode when the device opens.
It restores this mode after the parent device resumes.
Suspend clears pending taps and releases held buttons.
The first contact sets the motion origin.
It does not move the pointer until a subsequent contact report arrives.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
Each device provides
.Va hw.imtN.tapping .
The default value is zero.
Set it to one to enable single-finger tap clicks.
Taps longer than 180 milliseconds do not click.
Motion beyond 50 native coordinate units cancels the tap.
Multiple fingers, a physical button press, or a low-confidence contact also
cancel the tap.
.Pp
With tapping enabled,
.Va hw.imtN.tapping_drag
set to one holds the left button after a tap for 250 milliseconds.
A new single-finger contact in this time drags with the button held.
The button releases when that contact lifts.
A short second tap gives a double click.
A second finger ends the drag.
If the touchpad stops reporting during a drag for two seconds, the button
releases.
The default value is zero.
.Pp
.Va hw.imtN.three_finger_drag
set to one drags with three fingers.
The third finger must land within 200 milliseconds of the first.
Three contacts that stay for 80 milliseconds and whose mean position
moves 50 native coordinate units from where the third finger landed press
the left button.
The pointer does not move before the button goes down.
The tracked contact then moves the pointer.
When fingers lift one by one, the pointer stops.
The button releases when the last finger lifts.
A fourth finger before the press, or a touch that scrolled or had four
fingers, does not drag until every finger is lifted, so four-finger swipes
still work.
A fourth finger after the press keeps the drag.
Three contacts that come back more than 200 milliseconds after the first
finger landed do not arm again until every finger is lifted.
A touch that arms a drag does not start a three-finger swipe.
A physical click with three fingers before the press is a middle click;
during the drag it stays a left click.
If the touchpad stops reporting during a drag for two seconds, the button
releases.
This setting does not depend on
.Va hw.imtN.tapping .
The default value is zero.
.Pp
Use
.Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
to preserve the setting across boots.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ihidev 4 ,
.Xr wsmouse 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The driver uses the Windows Precision Touchpad report model from
.Ox
.Nm
and
.Nm hidmt .
This implementation uses the
.Nx
HID parser and wscons pointer interface.
